Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(viewer+dogfood):=20fit-to-content=20zoom,?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20border-true=20arrows,=20level=20tally=20=E2=80=94=20and=20a?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20self-model=20that=20shows=20it?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gap left after Track A was not machinery but presence: the self-model
rendered as one lonely green box in a fixed 1020px canvas, while the
hand-made status boards read dense, coloured and alive. Three viewer fixes
and one dogfood pass close it.

Viewer:
- fit-to-content viewBox: the level shrink-wraps its nodes and label
  anchors (minimums stop a single box from becoming comically large;
  slack is split evenly so content stays centred). Export backgrounds
  honour the fitted origin.
- edge endpoints trim at the true rectangle border, not a radial guess -
  on wide boxes with shallow angles the old trim landed inside the box
  and dragged the label under the node. Falls back to the radial trim
  when boxes touch. Labels gain a stage-coloured paint-order halo.
- per-level programme tally in the breadcrumb: status dots + mean
  completion, computed on real children so the catalogue threshold can
  never change the numbers. Description cap 3 -> 4 lines, still
  geometry-driven.

Dogfood (the essence): the self-model now uses every channel the engine
grew in 0.4.0 - a curated context level (developer/agent, target
codebase, npm registry, CI+Pages, planned status boards), a real
programme overlay in c4-status.json, layout hints for L1/L2, meta.title.
The Pages demo finally shows what the tool can do instead of proving it
was never pointed at itself.

Test fallout: the attach fixture regenerates a synthetic topology over a
copy of the self-repo, so it drops the repo's REAL overlay first - gen
failing loud on ids the synthetic topology never had is correct.

npm test green (12 suites), lint green, forma check green.

